        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add process and SQLite lock diagnostics",
        "body": "Closes #86.\n\nAdds `gitcrawl doctor --locks --json` for read-only SQLite diagnostics: DB/WAL/SHM/journal state, read-only open status, quick-check status, safe inspection status, and best-effort process detection.\n\nPlatforms without supported process inspection now report that limitation explicitly instead of treating missing process data as proof that no writer exists.\n\nBehavior proof:\nOn a throwaway archive synced for `openclaw/gitcrawl#86`, lock diagnostics reported `db_exists: true`, `read_only_open: \"ok\"`, `quick_check: \"ok\"`, and `safe_read_only_inspection: true`.\n\n\nPortable-store proof after repair:\nA throwaway portable-store config now reports the configured checkout DB at top level and the runtime mirror for lock inspection.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"db_path\": \".../checkout/data/openclaw__openclaw.sync.db\",\n  \"locks_db_path\": \".../runtime/checkout/data/openclaw__openclaw.sync.db\",\n  \"source_exists\": true,\n  \"runtime_exists\": true,\n  \"safe_read_only_inspection\": true,\n  \"quick_check\": \"ok\"\n}\n```\n",
        "branch": "lock-diagnostics-86",
